<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech SPIF Cesky says FinMin supports move to open.</title>
<headline>Czech SPIF Cesky says FinMin supports move to open.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>SPIF Cesky, the second largest Czech investment fund, on Tuesday said the Finance Ministry had given preliminary support to change into an open-ended fund, despite Czech laws forbidding the move.</p>
<p>&quot;The Ministry, after basic preliminary consultations on the possibility to transform investment fund into an open-ended fund, has voiced its support,&quot; a SPIF Cesky statement said.</p>
<p>The statement did not elaborate further.</p>
</text>
